      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Critics argue that many DEI programs are focused on \"tokenism\" or \"greenwashing,\" where organizations publicly promote diversity and inclusion without making meaningful changes to their policies, practices, or hiring processes. Research suggests that these superficial efforts can actually lead to a decrease in Employee Engagement and Attendance, particularly if benefits aren't tailored to specific staff populations. This reinforces the notion that some DEI initiatives may be more performative than genuinely impactful.",
